! v0.73.0 PCM test 3:  methanol in water (HF/STO-3G, C-PCM).
!
! Different molecule than tests 1-2:  exercises a 6-atom system with
! mixed elements (C, O, H) so the Bondi-radius lookup is non-trivial,
! and the cavity has more spheres to taper across.  Methanol's larger
! dipole moment (~1.7 D for the gas-phase molecule) should give a
! noticeably stronger solvation than water in water on a molar basis,
! though the comparison is geometry-dependent and not a strict test.
!
! Geometry: HF/STO-3G optimized methanol (literature, 1986 vintage).
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%pcm     cpcm     ! v0.74+ default is iefpcm; v0.73 tests pin cpcm explicitly
%solvent water
%geom angstrom
C   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
O   1.388000   0.000000   0.000000
H  -0.354000   0.957000   0.367000
H  -0.354000  -0.957000   0.367000
H  -0.430000   0.000000  -1.020000
H   1.700000   0.910000   0.000000
*end
